<%# What an answer replaces. The element around it persists and carries both the
    Stimulus controller and the `aria-live` region, so a change of state is
    announced rather than silently swapped in — a region replaced along with its
    contents announces nothing.

    `data-polling` is how the zone tells the controller whether to ask again: a
    settled zone says `false`, and the asking stops because the server said so.
    `data-outcome` says what happened, which is another question — a refusal and
    a document both stop the asking. The card above reads it, having no other way
    to learn what became of a click it does not hold, and so does the controller,
    which replaces nothing while the answer says what the zone already says: the
    waiting is one waiting, and one announcement. %>
<div class="demo-request__body" data-polling="<%= pending? %>" data-outcome="<%= state %>">
  <% if delivered? %>
    <%# Chapter 1 §4.2: the evidence is « made available to the specific
        procedure end-user that issued the query », and the user « cannot modify
        its content in any way » — so it is offered exactly as it arrived. %>
    <%= link_to t('components.demo_request_zone.open'), evidence_path,
          class: 'fr-btn fr-btn--secondary fr-btn--icon-left fr-icon-attachment-line',
          target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener', lang: 'en' %>

    <p class="fr-mb-0 demo-request__state" lang="en">
      <span class="fr-icon-check-line demo-request__check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <%= t('components.demo_request_zone.delivered') %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <%# `button_to` and not a link: chapter 4.5.1 §2.3 allows the `IssueDateTime`
        no material distance from this gesture, and a GET the browser prefetched
        would issue it before the user had decided anything.

        Rendered while the answer is out too, and merely hidden: the button
        reappears whenever the server renders a settled zone, and a fragment
        that left it out would have none to show. Nothing in the browser brings
        it back — giving up offers a way back to the page instead, clicking
        again being a second exchange (chapter 4.4 §4.1). %>
    <%= button_to submit_label, button_path,
          class: 'fr-btn fr-btn--icon-left fr-icon-arrow-down-circle-line', lang: 'en',
          form: { class: 'demo-request__button', hidden: pending?,
                  data: { demo_request_target: 'button' } } %>

    <%# Rendered beside the button and hidden, rather than waited for: a click
        is answered a round trip away, and a screen that says nothing until the
        answer comes back leaves the user clicking again. The controller shows
        this and hides the button. The waiting the server then sends is this same
        one — the controller leaves it standing rather than building it again —
        and the wording is the server's throughout: no English lives in the
        Stimulus controller. %>
    <%= tag.p class: 'fr-mb-0 demo-request__state demo-request__state--waiting', lang: 'en',
          hidden: !pending?, data: { demo_request_target: 'loading' } do %>
      <span class="demo-request__spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <%= t('components.demo_request_zone.loading') %>
    <% end %>

    <%# What the browser raises on its own when it gets no answer it can use — a
        network that dropped, or something that answered without the header this
        application sets. The server cannot say that it cannot be reached, so the
        sentence is rendered here, hidden, and the controller shows it. %>
    <%= tag.p class: 'fr-mb-0 demo-request__state demo-request__state--waiting', lang: 'en',
          hidden: true, data: { demo_request_target: 'disconnected' } do %>
      <span class="fr-icon-error-warning-line demo-request__failed" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <%= t('components.demo_request_zone.disconnected_html',
            reload: link_to(t('components.demo_request_zone.reload'), helpers.admin_demo_documents_path)) %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <% if failed? %>
    <%# Chapter 2.1 §3.3 has the user told that the evidence cannot be provided;
        the code below says which refusal it was, and the component the journal
        uses glosses it. Hidden the moment the button is clicked again: what it
        reports is no longer what is happening. %>
    <%# `lang="fr"`: the title comes from `interactors.failures.*`, which the
        operator console shares with this screen and which is written in French —
        the one piece of this zone that is not in English. Said rather than left
        to be pronounced as English (RGAA 8.7). %>
    <div class="demo-request__failure" data-demo-request-target="failure" lang="fr">
      <%= helpers.dsfr_alert(type: :error, title: failure_title) do %>
        <%= failure_body %>
        <% if edm_error_code %>
          <%= render EdmErrorCodeComponent.new(code: edm_error_code) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
